# HYUNJUN — "One More Stop" (expansion)
# Six chapters between hyunjun_route and act4_choice, the final beat, and two new endings.
# Conceit: ECHO's clock was 1h47 fast. The night he finally let end is handed back, and he has
#   to decide what to do with time he isn't afraid of losing.
# Motif: a line map drawn on a convenience-store receipt. Lines have last stops. Lines get extended.
# Flags: hyunjunx_map, hyunjunx_ate, hyunjunx_held, hyunjunx_box, hyunjunx_reply, hyunjunx_blank

=== hyunjun_ch1
@autosave
@bg studio_hall t=fade
@music quiet
@time 04:57
@amb room
@show hyunjun smile at=c
> You take the stairs slowly. Not on purpose. He stops on every step as if each one were a station.
> Halfway down, the lights in the stairwell flicker once, the way a person clears their throat.
@textbox echo
echo: All recipients. Before you gather, I have an error to report.
echo: At 00:41 the storm cut my power for nine seconds. When I restarted, I set my clock from the wall clock behind the front desk.
echo: I have now compared it with the power company's signal. The wall clock is one hour and forty-seven minutes fast.
echo: I am told it has been that way since a battery change. Nobody fixed it. Everybody simply subtracted.
echo: It is not 04:57. It is 03:10.
@time 03:10
echo: My power will still be cut at 05:00. Their clock is correct. Mine was not. I am sorry.
echo: I am also, I think, pleased. Please disregard the last five times I said "almost."
@textbox normal
> Downstairs, somebody cheers. Somebody else, Songha by the sound of it, says the word *reschedule* the way other people say grace.
@expr hyunjun thinking
hyunjun: ...
hyunjun: No.
hyunjun: No. I did it. I let it end, and I was calm about it. You saw. It's the most composed I've been all year.
> He sits down on the stair, all at once, the way he sat on the taped seat.
hyunjun[smile]: And it hands it back. An hour and forty-seven minutes. Here, you dropped this.
hyunjun[thinking]: Is that how it works? You stop holding on, and you get more? Nobody told me. I'd have let go of a lot of things.
