    > He crosses out the cat with the solemnity of someone lowering a flag. Ten more lines go after it, faster.
    hyunjun[smile]: Okay. It's actually easier once the cat's gone. The cat was holding the whole list up.
* [quiet] Fold the receipt so only the top few lines show.
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    > You take it gently, crease it under the third stop, and hand it back. The other eleven are still there. They're just underneath now.
    hyunjun[thinking]: You didn't even cross them out.
    hyunjun[smile]: They still exist. They're just not tonight. I didn't know that was a category.
> He turns the receipt over to the clean end and draws a line down it. Straight. A small circle at the top.
hyunjun: Okay. New map. Proper one.
you: Not a loop?
hyunjun[thinking]: No. I thought about it. Line 2 is a circle, and I love it, and I rode it for four years.
hyunjun: This one's a line. Lines have a last stop. You can see it coming, and you still get on.
> He draws the circles as he names them, and writes each name beside its circle in small, fast capitals.
hyunjun: One. The lounge. The bag. It's a rescue mission. I'm not leaving a man behind, and the man is snacks.
hyunjun: Two. The practice room. There's a thing in there I can't do. I'll explain when we're standing in it.
hyunjun: Three. The roof. No reason. That's the reason.
@textbox echo
echo: If there is room on your line, I would like to request a stop.
echo: Basement. The archive. There is a part of RECORD 05 that I did not play. I was instructed not to. I would like to ask again.
@textbox normal
