    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    > A grey scuff, fresh, at the end of a line of older scuffs. All the same length. All pointing at the door.
    hyunjun[thinking]: ...That's me. Those are all me. I've been leaving in the same direction for a year.
> He sits down on the floor with his back against the mirror. His reflection sits back to back with him, like a colleague on the same shift.
hyunjun: I'll tell you why it's on my mind tonight. It's a real one. There's no joke in it.
you: Say it.
hyunjun[thinking]: Someday there's going to be a stage. A real one. Maybe. Nobody's promised. I know that. We all know that.
hyunjun: And I can see it. I know exactly what I'll do. I'll get the best three minutes of my life, and I'll walk out of them on five.
hyunjun[thinking]: I'll be thinking about the next thing. And the thing I've waited for since I was fourteen will be behind me, and I'll have *left early*.
> He picks at the lace of one sneaker. It's pink. It's double-knotted.
hyunjun: And there's a harder part. I'd like to say it to you.
hyunjun: I want it to be with them. These seven. Exactly these.
hyunjun: You're not supposed to want it that specifically. Nothing's decided. You're supposed to want the general thing. The general thing is safe.
hyunjun: I don't want the general thing. I want Justin stealing my water. I want Songha's schedule taped to a dressing room door.
hyunjun[thinking]: Wanting it that much frightens me a little. Once I say it, there's something to lose.
