    hyunjun[smile]: That's the most useful thing anyone's said to me all year. Everyone else promises the stage.
> He gets up. Shakes his arms out. Stands on his mark.
hyunjun: Okay. Help. How do people stay in a thing that's over? You're the expert. You're the one who always gets off on time.
> You think about that. About trains. About how you were, in fact, never in a hurry on them.
you: I didn't just leave. I told you. I said all the names first. One more time each. Then I was allowed to go.
hyunjun[thinking]: Bye, river.
you: Bye, river. So don't hold still for eight counts. Holding still is hard. Say goodbye for eight counts. One thing per count.
you: Whatever was in the three minutes. Name it. When you've run out of names, you can walk.
> He stares at you.
hyunjun: That's — hang on. That's not staying. That's *leaving properly*.
hyunjun[smile]: Nobody told me there was a properly.
> You stand where a camera would be, by the speaker stack. He looks at you, then at the mirror, then decides on you.
* [sincere] "I'll count. Out loud. You do the names in your head."
    @rel hyunjun trust+1
    hyunjun[smile]: Out loud. Good. If it's out loud, I can't pretend I didn't hear five.
* [playful] "I'm the camera. I have a red light. I don't blink."
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[smile]: You blinked. You blinked just then.
    you: Technical fault.
    hyunjun[laugh]: Worst camera I've ever worked with. Stay right there.
