you: Six.
> *Thief*, his mouth says. *Schedule.*
you: Seven.
> His arm is shaking a little. He's breathing like someone who's run up from the platform. He's looking straight at you.
you: Eight.
> He doesn't move.
> You don't say nine. There isn't a nine. He holds it anyway, one more count, two, smiling now with his arm still up, until the laugh gets out.
